1f:["$","$L8","reality-3d",{"variant":"scale","children":["$","$L1e",null,{"project":{"id":"reality-3d","href":"/engineering/reality-3d","name":"Reality 3D","category":"Independent | 3D Commerce Platform","url":"https://reality3d.in","urlDisplay":"reality3d.in","repo":"https://github.com/kasai22/sada3d-world","description":"Designed and developed a 3D-printing commerce experience with product discovery and customer-facing manufacturing workflows; implemented front-end features and backend/API integrations.","objective":"An on-demand manufacturing storefront: browse a catalogue of printable products, or upload your own model, inspect it in 3D and get a manufacturing quote — with what can and cannot be made stated plainly to the customer.","stack":["Next.js 16 (App Router)","React 19","TypeScript","three.js (WebGL)","Payload CMS 3","PostgreSQL · Drizzle","Supabase Auth","S3-compatible object storage"],"accent":"#3D4FA0","image":{"src":"/engineering/reality3d.png","alt":"Reality 3D home page — Manufacturing, reimagined: turn digital designs into physical products","width":1440,"height":900},"ownership":{"designed":["Product discovery: catalogue browse, filter, search and sort, each with empty, loading and error states.","The custom-print workflow: upload, analyse, configure, quote.","A capability model customers can read — available, coming soon, unavailable — so nothing unapprovable can be quoted or ordered.","An operations console for orders, customers, designs, production and issues."],"implemented":["One WebGL viewer behind an imperative engine class: React owns mounting, teardown and controls; the engine owns everything on the GPU.","Format loaders for STL, OBJ and glTF/GLB, each imported on demand.","A deterministic exploded view — pure maths, no randomness — so a model separates identically on every load.","A quote engine with request validation and pricing rules, plus cart, checkout, guest order tracking and the account area."],"integrated":["Payload CMS as the catalogue and admin back end, on PostgreSQL with Drizzle migrations.","Supabase authentication for customer accounts.","S3-compatible object storage with presigned URLs for uploaded model files.","Route handlers for quotes, models, designs, orders, checkout and health checks."],"aiAssisted":["Built in documented phases with AI coding assistance (Claude); each phase was reviewed, tested and committed separately.","A self-run production audit and screen-and-state inventory record what is verified and what is not, rather than assuming generated code works."]},"challenges":[{"problem":"Customers upload STEP files, which are a boundary representation, not a mesh.","approach":"The custom-print analysis says so plainly — dimensions and volume cannot be measured from surfaces — while the file can still be quoted and manufactured, instead of failing silently."},{"problem":"An exploded view that rearranges itself between viewings is not a drawing anyone can read.","approach":"Explosion directions are pure and deterministic — radial from the assembly centre, with fixed fallback axes by scene order for centred parts."},{"problem":"The storefront must never sell a material or process the business has not approved.","approach":"Capability status comes from a business decision ledger; the quote engine, cart, checkout and order creation all refuse anything not approved."}],"validation":["Unit and stress tests on Node's built-in test runner — pricing, catalogue, cart and checkout, orders, security, storage, geometry and the viewer's maths.","A written MVP production audit and screen-and-state inventory listing what is implemented, reachable and functional."],"deployment":"Deployed on Vercel.","excerpt":{"path":"src/lib/viewer/explode.ts","caption":"How a component travels in the exploded view — deterministic, so the same model explodes identically every time.","code":"export function explodeDirection(\n  component: ExplodeComponent,\n  assembly: AssemblyBounds,\n): Vector3 {\n  const radial = new Vector3().subVectors(component.center, assembly.center);\n  const threshold = Math.max(assembly.radius * CENTRED_EPSILON, Number.EPSILON);\n\n  if (radial.length() > threshold) return radial.normalize();\n\n  const axis = FALLBACK_AXES[component.index % FALLBACK_AXES.length];\n  // The table is non-empty and the index is taken modulo its length.\n  return axis ? axis.clone() : new Vector3(0, 1, 0);\n}"},"limits":["Checkout runs on a mock payment adapter — no live payment provider is integrated yet."]}}]}]
20:["$","$L8","hotelfirst",{"variant":"scale","children":["$","$L1e",null,{"project":{"id":"hotelfirst","href":"/engineering/hotelfirst","name":"HotelFirst","category":"Independent | Business Website","url":"https://hotelfirst.one","urlDisplay":"hotelfirst.one","description":"Designed, developed and deployed a responsive business website, translating service needs into clear information architecture and customer-facing page journeys.","objective":"A website for a hotel-owner advisory and asset-strategy practice: explain the services clearly, and give a hotel owner an obvious path from reading to getting in touch.","stack":["Next.js","Tailwind CSS","Vercel"],"accent":"#B4430A","image":{"src":"/figmaAssets/hotelfirst-screenshot.png","alt":"HotelFirst advisory website home page","width":1440,"height":900},"ownership":{"designed":["Information architecture that turns a list of advisory services into page journeys a hotel owner can follow.","Content hierarchy and calls to action for each page."],"implemented":["A responsive front end — layouts that hold from phone to desktop.","Statically prerendered pages for fast first load."],"integrated":["Deployment and hosting on Vercel."]},"challenges":[],"deployment":"Deployed on Vercel as a prerendered Next.js site."}}]}]
21:["$","$L8","portfolio",{"variant":"scale","children":["$","$L1e",null,{"project":{"id":"portfolio","href":"/engineering/portfolio","name":"Personal Portfolio","category":"Independent | Design & Development","url":"https://chsaikomal.site","urlDisplay":"chsaikomal.site","repo":"https://github.com/kasai22/saikomal_portfolio","description":"Built and maintain a portfolio showcasing product case studies, design decisions and hands-on web development work.","objective":"One site that has to work as a design portfolio and as a front-end code sample at the same time — so the way it is built is part of what it shows.","stack":["Next.js 16 (App Router)","React 19","TypeScript","Tailwind CSS","Motion","GSAP ScrollTrigger","Lenis","Vercel"],"accent":"#8A5A0A","image":{"src":"/engineering/portfolio.png","alt":"This portfolio's home page","width":1440,"height":900},"ownership":{"designed":["The visual system — an editorial paper-and-ink palette, a display grotesque with a mono annotation layer, and one section rhythm used everywhere.","Long-form case studies with a contents rail, and five scroll-driven figures that explain the practice — how design, engineering and AI combine, how an interface is assembled, an AI product loop, how a problem gets ordered, and the method as one machine."],"implemented":["Feature-folder architecture: each case study owns its components and content; shared case-study primitives sit in one place.","Every fact — dates, metrics, contact details, projects — read from two typed content modules, so nothing is duplicated.","Motion that honours the reduced-motion preference everywhere: pinned, scroll-driven figures fall back to a static, fully written-out sequence on phones and under reduced motion — and GSAP is never downloaded there.","A contents rail that builds itself from the headings on the page, so a new section is indexed without being registered."],"integrated":["Static generation for every route, metadata, sitemap and schema.org JSON-LD, deployed on Vercel."],"aiAssisted":["Claude is used as a coding partner — for audits, refactors and first drafts — with every change reviewed, built and checked in the browser before it ships."]},"challenges":[{"problem":"The same employment dates and metrics appeared in a timeline, cards, metadata and case studies, and drifted out of sync.","approach":"Moved every fact into one typed source with structured dates and a single formatter; the pages derive their copy from it."},{"problem":"The hero headline is the page's largest paint, and a fade-in entrance kept it from counting as painted until hydration finished.","approach":"The headline reveal is a mask, not a fade: the text is fully opaque from the first frame and rises from behind its own clip box, so the entrance costs nothing in Largest Contentful Paint."},{"problem":"The hero's project tiles had to travel into the real case-study cards below without a second copy of either ever being on screen.","approach":"A sibling layer measures both ends each frame and flies one tile at a time, hiding only the element it is standing in for — and below tablet width, or under reduced motion, nothing flies at all."}],"deployment":"Deployed on Vercel; every route statically generated.","excerpt":{"path":"constants/profile.ts","caption":"Dates are stored structured and formatted in one place, so no page carries its own copy.","code":"/** \"November 2024 – May 2026\", \"May 2026 – Present\". */\nexport function formatPeriod(role: Pick<Employment, \"start\" | \"end\">, short = false): string {\n  const end = role.end ? formatYearMonth(role.end, short) : \"Present\";\n  return `${formatYearMonth(role.start, short)} – ${end}`;\n}"}}}]}]
